description:
Design a dual-edge-triggered flip-flop that captures input data based on both the rising and falling edges of the clock signal. It consists of two pipeline stages where the first stage captures the input data `d` on the rising edge of `clk`, while the second stage updates the output `q` based on the previous stage's values and the input data on the falling edge of `clk`. This configuration effectively allows the flip-flop to sample data continuously across the clock edges, enhancing data throughput in digital circuits.
module top_module(
    input clk,
    input d,
    output q
);

code:
module top_module(
    input clk,
    input d,
    output q
);reg d1, d2;
reg q1, q2;

// Pipeline stage 1
always @(posedge clk) begin
    d1 <= d;
    q1 <= q2;
end

// Pipeline stage 2
always @(negedge clk) begin
    d2 <= q1;
    q2 <= d1 ^ q1;
end

assign q = q2;

endmodule

